# {{ projectName }} architecture

`create_app` is the composition root. A FastAPI lifespan owns each worker's resources and closes them after partial startup or normal shutdown. Imports do not create configured resources. Health routes use `APIRouter`; product routers belong to the application.

{% if withPersistence %}The request dependency owns a short transaction and commits or rolls back before the response is sent. Handlers and repositories do not commit. Serialize ORM data before cleanup; never share an `AsyncSession` between tasks. Keep external I/O outside a transaction. Streaming, WebSocket and background work need their own resource scope. Alembic revisions are application-owned and run explicitly, separately from replica startup.{% else %}Persistence is disabled; no engine, session, DSN or database readiness call is created.{% endif %}

{% if withTesting %}Ordinary HTTP/configuration/error/lifecycle tests use `with TestClient(application) as client`, with a new app and settings for each test. Only an expected handled HTTP 500 disables propagation. The actual async PostgreSQL transaction/readiness acceptance uses HTTPX `AsyncClient` and explicit lifespan in one event loop. TestClient does not receive another loop's session or pool. Real database integration is separate from isolated tests; synthetic connection-boundary fakes are not evidence of PostgreSQL availability.

Managed tests use `tests/foundation`; application-owned tests remain in their existing paths. Coverage measures every own runtime module, including modules not imported by the suite, and requires complete statements and branches. Installed-wheel container tests run from `/checks`, outside the build source path. Test assets
include project-owned tools and migration files, while `src/` is explicitly excluded and the
package test verifies its installed origin. `make test` starts with a new integration coverage
measurement on a disposable DB, then appends isolated execution and applies the full gate; a
restored or previous report cannot replace current tests. Root `tests/*_integration.py` files are
included so project-owned migration cases survive updates.
{% endif %}

{% if withDocker %}The Docker recipe separates locked dependencies, wheel build, test environment and minimal runtime. BuildKit layer reuse follows actual inputs; tests rerun after a cached solve. Runtime contains the installed wheel and production dependencies, without compiler, Git, uv or the test runner. UID 65532 and normalized read permissions support restrictive source umasks and a read-only runtime filesystem.
{% endif %}{% if withKubernetes %}

The FastAPI base owns the managed Helm chart. Deployments have independent liveness/readiness/startup probes, bounded resources, no service-account token mount, no extra capabilities and a read-only filesystem. An optional migration hook uses the same image and an existing Secret. Chart upgrades and rollbacks use an already tested artifact; they do not reverse historical database changes. `.local/kubeconfig` belongs only to the disposable local contour and is ignored by Git.
{% endif %}

Project-owned Make commands belong in `Makefile.local`; the common Makefile includes it without
copying shared recipes. `HTTP_HOST`, `HTTP_PORT` and `UVICORN_FLAGS` customize the local `make run`
command. Production container arguments stay fixed and do not inherit development reload flags.
